cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Sensor Fusion Lab
message: If you use this lab or its figures, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jabbala
    given-names: Gunasekar
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-24"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jabbala10-bit/sensor-fusion-lab"
abstract: >-
  Nine from-scratch programs teaching sensor fusion for autonomous systems:
  lidar obstacle detection (RANSAC, KD-tree, Euclidean clustering, L-shape box
  fitting), camera geometry and time to collision (Harris, SIFT, descriptor
  matching, IoU and NMS), FMCW radar (range-Doppler processing, 2D CA-CFAR,
  angle of arrival, GNN multi-target tracking) and Kalman filtering (KF, EKF
  with Jacobians, UKF with the CTRV model, NIS consistency). Every lab
  simulates its own sensor, so no dataset is required.
keywords:
  - sensor-fusion
  - autonomous-driving
  - lidar
  - radar
  - computer-vision
  - kalman-filter
  - unscented-kalman-filter
  - ransac
  - cfar
  - multi-target-tracking
